# Smart City STEM Education Model

This project presents a **Smart City model designed to support STEM education for teenagers and young learners**. It provides a hands-on environment where students can explore concepts related to technology, science, engineering, programming, sustainability, and urban innovation.

The project is organized in two complementary repositories:

* **Smart City Model - Version 1(#)** — Basic operation of the modules, 3D-printed design, MQTT communications, AI-based visual computing. Link: https://github.com/Rui-Martins31/Smart_City_Model/tree/main
* **Smart City Model - Version 2(#)** — Updated model operation, digital twin module. Link: https://gitlab.com/engenharia_de_sistemas_25_26/engenharia_de_sistemas_25_26

Together, these two repositories provide the required files to replicate the Smart City Model described in the paper "Enhancing STEM Education Through a 3D-Printed Smart City Model and Affordable Electronic Components", published in the IEEE Smart Cities 2026 conference (https://dei.fe.up.pt/ieee-isc2-2026/)
